---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Checked from '../../components/Checked.astro';
import Crumbs from '../../components/Crumbs.astro';
import Newsletter from '../../components/Newsletter.astro';
import { formatDate } from '../../lib/formatDate';
import { handsOnNotes, assertHandsOnCoverage } from '../../lib/handsOnNotes';
import { hubPage } from '../../lib/hubPage';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/withBase';

const entries = await getCollection('use-cases', ({ data }) => !data.draft);
assertHandsOnCoverage(entries);
const titles = new Map(entries.map((entry) => [entry.id, entry.data.title]));
const title = 'Tested by us';
const description = 'Hands-on notes: Consensus, Perplexity, DeepL, LanguageTool, Looka, Phrasly, Datastripes, nixm, Dessn, Spacefast, Quillo, signed-out Pixelcut and Photoroom.';
const notes = [...handsOnNotes].sort((a, b) => b.date.localeCompare(a.date));
const hub = hubPage(
  Astro.site!,
  Astro.url.pathname,
  title,
  description,
  notes.map((note) => ({ name: note.tool, path: `/use-cases/${note.useCaseSlug}/` })),
);
---
<Base title={title} description={description} jsonLd={hub.jsonLd} hasNewsletter>
  <article class="wrap narrow" data-pagefind-body>
    <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom:8px">
      <Crumbs items={[{ href: withBase('/'), label: 'Home' }, { label: title }]} />
      <span class="eyebrow">Hands-on notes</span>
      <h1>Tested by us</h1>
      <p class="lead">These are the only hands-on notes written on the site. Each one names the date, the tool, and what was actually tried. A shorter check does not turn the use-case page into a completed test.</p>
      <div class="meta"><Checked date={hub.dateModified} label={hub.dateLabel} /></div>
    </section>

    <section class="answer" aria-labelledby="short-answer">
      <h2 id="short-answer">Short answer</h2>
      <p>Twelve notes exist. Consensus Free on 26 Oct 2026 and Perplexity Free on 2 Nov 2026 are on the research page. DeepL Free on 3 Nov 2026 is on the translate page. LanguageTool Basic on 4 Nov 2026 is on the proofread page. Looka Brand Kit on 5 Nov 2026 is on the logo page. Phrasly AI Image Detector on 6 Nov 2026 is on the image-check page. Datastripes on 7 Nov 2026 is on the spreadsheet page. nixm on 8 Nov 2026 is on the writing page. Dessn on 9 Nov 2026 is on the app-screen page. Spacefast on 10 Nov 2026 is on the vibe-code page. Quillo on 11 Nov 2026 is on the voiceover page. Pixelcut and Photoroom, signed out, on 14 Nov 2026 are on the product-photo page. No other tool on this site has a hands-on note.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The notes</h2>
      <div class="verdicts">
        {notes.map((note) => {
          const useCaseTitle = titles.get(note.useCaseSlug);
          if (!useCaseTitle) throw new Error(`Missing title for ${note.useCaseSlug}`);
          return (
            <article class="card">
              <div class="meta" style="margin-top:0">
                <span class="tag tested">Hands-on note <time datetime={note.date}>{formatDate(new Date(`${note.date}T00:00:00.000Z`))}</time></span>
              </div>
              <h3 style="font-size:1.2rem;margin-top:10px">{note.tool}</h3>
              <p>{note.tested}</p>
              <p class="caveat">{note.limits}</p>
              <p><a href={withBase(`/use-cases/${note.useCaseSlug}/`)}>{useCaseTitle}</a></p>
            </article>
          );
        })}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>What this page is not</h2>
      <p>The research page, the translate page, the proofread page, the logo page, the image-check page, the spreadsheet page and the writing page stay marked pending. Their standard tasks have not been run. The slide-deck page, the vibe-code page, the app-screen page, the voiceover page and the product-photo page stay marked pending. Consensus Pro, Elicit, Gemini Notebook, DeepL Pro Individual, Grammarly Pro, Canva Pro, Google Sheets, Claude, ChatGPT, Bolt.new, Lovable, Figma, v0, ElevenLabs, Descript and every pick that is not named above have no hands-on note. None of them has a completed standard-task note. The Looka Brand Kit note is the free logo maker, the editor, the mockup previews and the checkout prices. The paid kit was not bought, no file was downloaded, and a 1080×1080 social graphic was not made. The Phrasly note is five images on the free detector, signed out: two real photos read Likely real, two AI JPEGs were caught by a signature in the file, and the ChatGPT ramen example showed a SynthID watermark and OpenAI's signature. Pixel detection did not run on those AI files. Phrasly's over 99% accuracy figure is the vendor's claim and was not measured. A separate signature-free Midjourney-style file was not tested. The Datastripes note is one signed-out upload of a 20-row CSV. Export and saving need a sign-up. The privacy line on the page, that rows stay in the browser, was not checked by network inspection. The nixm note is one signed-out chat draft on nixm.ai. A still image needed an account and was not generated. No shareable NIXM URL appeared. Magic-link signup, the stated 20-credit grant, video, web research and signed-in stills were not tested. Vendor pages claim logged-out signals are public by link and dissolve after seven days, and some copy says a still can be made without an account. Those claims were not verified. The Dessn note is one Free-plan screen at create.dessn.ai, signed in with an email link and no card. The first frame was about 2 minutes 6 seconds after the prompt. The names, prices, steppers and £10.10 total matched the quantities on screen. Placeholder copy was added, including "Baked this morning on Mill Lane". One step showed "1 action failed" and then the screen rendered. 20 credits were still showing, and Dessn said "This first one is on us", so the credit cost was not confirmed. No export or download control was seen. Figma and v0 were not part of it. The Spacefast note is one anonymous publish, with no account, of an existing two-file HTML page. sf publish . took about 4 seconds. A one-line redeploy took about 3.2 seconds and the change was live on the first check. The plain URL returned HTTP 403, "This space is private", and the page was viewable only through a private link. The anonymous space was set to expire in about 33 hours. Making it public needs a WordPress.com account and was not tested. A plain http:// request returned HTTP 500 instead of redirecting. The pricing figures are from the vendor page. Lovable, Bolt.new and Replit were not part of it. The Quillo note is one signed-out read-aloud on quillo.tr/text-to-speech, with no account and no card. The text was "Hollow Oak Bakery opens at 7:30 on 14/03. Call 020 7946 0018; sourdough is £4.50." The first Listen opened the reader in 1.105 seconds and did not start playback. The reader's Listen was pressed at 10:59:59.412 UTC, and Pause appeared within 0.566 seconds. Sentence 1 was highlighted yellow, and the counter moved from 1/2 to 2/2 by 11:00:09. Audio could not be heard in the test environment, so pronunciation of the time, date, phone number and price is unverified. Playback was confirmed from the player UI only. Signed out, the voices were device voices only: Automatic, Google UK English Female, Google UK English Male and Google US English, with no lock icons. Speeds were 0.8, 0.9, 1, 1.1, 1.25, 1.5, 1.75 and 2x, and 1.25x was selected. A FAQ on the page says device-voice reading has no length limit, and MP3 download is not available on this page. Natural Quillo voices need an account and were not tested. The listen-to-PDF page was opened and not playback-tested. Prices seen on 11 Nov 2026: Free $0; a one-time sign-in trial of 10 cloud minutes and 10 AI pages, no card; Starter $4.99/mo (30 cloud minutes and 15 AI pages a month) or $34.99/yr (20 minutes and 10 pages a month); Pro $9.99/mo (90 minutes and 40 pages a month) or $69.99/yr (60 minutes and 25 pages a month). US prices, and purchases are via mobile app stores. ElevenLabs and Descript were not part of it. The 14 Nov 2026 note is one signed-out check of the free web background removers, in the box browser, with no account, no email, no password, no card and no social sign-in. Optional cookies were rejected. The photo was a Highgrove Royal Garden honey jar, CC BY 4.0, from Wikimedia Commons, resized to 1200×1433. Pixelcut opened the editor at /ai-image-editor?tool=removeBackground. The editor controls appeared 0.85 seconds after upload, and the cut-out was visible within about 1 to 2 seconds. The signed-out download was a PNG at 904×1080, the option labelled Preview resolution 904×1080 Free. The other option was Full resolution 1200×1433 Free with sign in, and that sign-in path was not tested. An upsell, Get Pro, was on the page. Photoroom's free web tool returned a result in a few seconds. A capture 1.5 seconds after upload still showed a loader, and the exact time was not measured. The signed-out download was a PNG at 1200×1433. The white swatch worked signed out. The optional Add background editor asked to log in or sign up and was not pursued. Both kept the gold lid, the amber glass, the honey and the label text (HIGHGROVE, Honey, ROYAL GARDEN, 250g e 8.8oz), and removed the yellow shelf. Neither showed a watermark. Edge quality looked similar at this size, and there was no formal edge-error count. Pixelcut showed a result faster. Photoroom's signed-out file was full resolution, and Pixelcut's was a reduced preview. Photoroom Pro and a Pixelcut Free account were not part of it.</p>
      <p>Prices elsewhere on the site are vendor figures with a source and a checked date. They are not measurements from these notes.</p>
      <p>Browse <a href={withBase('/use-cases/')}>all use cases</a>, <a href={withBase('/best/')}>all shortlists</a> and <a href={withBase('/about/')}>how we test</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="signup"><Newsletter /></section>
  </article>
</Base>
